Hi Sarah,

Sometimes that can happen if there are really high levels of smoothing required to run the model. Does the model without SNPs (i.e., run using usermodel or commonfactor) print any warnings to this effect? If not, nothing looks off in your code and it would be helpful for me to be able to troubleshoot with an example set of 5 SNPs that are producing the chi-square p-values near 0. If you could send the sumstats output for those 5 SNPs, the LDSC object, and the full set of code you are using to andrew.g...@colorado.edu. Of course, feel free to deidentify the phenotypes as you did in the userGWAS example you sent.

Best,
  Andrew

